    <string name="fb_tip_mentality">More attacking = more shots and goals, but more space behind your defence.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_passing">Short keeps the ball and is safer; direct reaches the box faster with more risk.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_tempo">Fast tempo creates chances quicker but causes more errors and fatigue.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_width">Wide play brings more crosses; narrow play crowds the middle.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_focus">Middle = through balls (vision, passing); flanks = crosses (crossing, heading).</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_pressing">High pressing wins the ball higher up but tires your players.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_defline">A high line squeezes the midfield but is open to balls in behind.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_marking">Man-marking shuts down strikers; clever movers can escape it.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_counter">Break quickly after winning the ball in your own half.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_offside">Catches runners more often; needs well-drilled defenders.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_time_wasting">When leading after the hour mark the team slows the game down.</string>
    <string name="fb_tip_hard_tackling">Wins more duels, but brings more fouls, cards and penalties.</string>
